{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080659-shophouse","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"market-town timber-jettied shophouse","rationale":"Second pass: I kept what already read well (the stone base, the ochre half-timbered upper storey on a 1-block jetty, the spruce gable roof with stepped stone verges) and fixed what read flat or unfinished. (1) Street front: the shopfronts are now properly recessed 1 behind the stone piers, each with a glazed display over a stallboard, a projecting counter shelf, an oak lintel, a slab awning, a sign on the y5 jetty beam, and hanging lanterns under oak corbels at every pier. Planters sit at the curb, so the ground floor invites you in. (2) Upper floor: the windows are recessed 1 block behind the green shutters, with flower boxes on upside-down stair brackets at +1, so the plaster plane has three depths instead of one. (3) The side faces were the largest plain surfaces. The upper sides now carry the same shutter-and-box window pairs, framed by corner and mid posts and a top plate. The stone ground sides get windows with stair sills and spruce shutters. (4) The roofline is resolved: the eaves overhang to z -2 and 12 over a stone-slab cornice band, the verges sit 1 block proud of a recessed gable, and the gables are timber-framed with a collar beam, a king post and two small windows. The ridge is capped. (5) The chimney was a stub; it is now a 2x2 stone stack rising 3 blocks above the ridge and capped with campfires. I made it 2x2 rather than the documented 2x1 so it reads from the street. The bakery is the x7-10 bay, so the chimney at x8-9 stands over its smoker and the doc's chimney position is honoured. The palette hierarchy is unchanged: stone carries the load, oak and spruce shape it, and green is the one accent. Both bays mirror each other."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:cobbl